-- chore/explicit-grants (D2): every Data API privilege our objects need, written explicitly.
-- New Supabase projects no longer auto-grant anon/authenticated/service_role on new public objects (changelog 45329), so the
-- grants the earlier migrations got implicitly from default privileges are stated here. Generated from the privilege set the
-- migrations produce on a stack WITH the old defaults (scripts/privilege-snapshot.sql, 307 lines), so it is exact parity: nothing
-- broader than today, append-only tables stay without UPDATE/DELETE/TRUNCATE for the Data API roles, `app` stays non-executable
-- for clients, and anon holds no table or function privilege. Grants are idempotent: a no-op on projects that already have them.
-- Contract: supabase/tests/070_privilege_contract.test.sql. A feature that adds an object adds its grants in its own migration and
-- extends that test's expected set (additions only). PUBLIC's schema USAGE is a PostgreSQL default and is not managed here.
-- Note: public.tenant and public.membership give service_role the full table set (as the old defaults did); parity kept on purpose.

